  "context": {
    "text": "What this study tests & why scores drop above 16k on a standard cloud server: We tested condensed chart budgets from 1k up to 128k tokens on a shared 24 GB cloud GPU. Because the standard Ollama server defaults to a 16k-token active working memory window, sending a 32k, 64k, or 128k chart causes the server to silently drop the beginning of the prompt\u2014cutting off the patient's active allergies, active medications, and recent 2025\u20132026 hospital admissions at the top of the chart. In a blinded 2-judge clinical review (Claude Opus 4.6 + GPT-5.4), plain chart summaries collapse from 80.2/100 at 8k down to 0.0\u20132.8/100 once that cutoff happens (with 4/4 unsafe answers), while Med Agent Hub (+ clinical rules & graph) leads at 88.0/100 with Gemma 4 26B at 8k (0 unsafe answers), beats raw at 1k (43.8 vs. 24.8/100), and still rescues the Part 1 medication conflicts above the cutoff (27.0\u201332.8/100) because its safety summary sits inside the active window at the end of the prompt.",
    "url": "https://openclinai.org/med-agent-hub/wahs-architecture/",
    "label": "How Med Agent Hub works \u2192"
  },
